kayak-fx26 0.1 — FX-26, the engine written in KFX (an interpreter over a heap of its own, collected)
(each entry runs while you type the next, its value %k after it; ^C interrupts the newest, ,help for more)
[Jfx26> ,help
[2K,help              this; ,help NAME: what NAME is
[2K,type E            E's type and effect, checked and not run
[2K,time E            E run, then its time, steps and collections
[2K,load FILE         FILE's forms, an entry
[2K,pending           the entries not ended
[2K,cancel K          entry K interrupted (^C: the newest)
[2K,step-limit [N|none]  how many steps an entry may take
[2K,apropos TEXT      the names containing TEXT
[2K,quit              leave now (^D: when every entry has ended)
[2KAnything else is forms, checked and run as an entry; %K is entry K's value;
[2Kan entry naming one that has not ended waits for it.
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> ,type (+ 1 2)
[2K(+ 1 2) : nat ! pure
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> ,time (+ 1 2)
[2K[1] 3 : nat ! pure  (0.0 s, 4 steps, 0 collections)
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> ,apropos string-app
[2Kstring-append
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> ,help string-append
[2Kstring-append : (subr pure (string string) string), a primitive
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> ,step-limit 5000
[2Kan entry may take 5000 steps
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> (define forever (subr (maxeff spin (read @globals)) (int) int) (lambda (n) (forever (+ n 1))))
[2K[2] forever : (subr (maxeff spin (read @globals)) (int) int) ! pure
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> (forever 0)
[2K[3] ! the step limit, 5000, reached (,step-limit)
[Jfx26> [Jfx26> ,step-limit none
